                    <div class="terms-section">
                    <div class="terms-heading">TERMS &amp; CONDITIONS OF THE CONTRACT</div>
                    
                    <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">1. Item Offered:</span> <strong>“UTKARSH” </strong>brand {!itemOffered}</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">2. Material Specification &amp; Price: </span> As per Annexure – 1.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">3. Freight:</span> {!freightBasis}</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">4. Packing &amp; Forwarding Charges:</span> {!packingForwarding}</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">5. Inspection:</span> {!inspectionTerms}</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">6. Loading &amp; Unloading charges:</span> {!loadingCharges}</div>
                        <div class="term-item">
                            <span class="term-title">7. Duties &amp; Taxes:</span>
                            <strong>7.a) GST:</strong> The rates are exclusive of GST @ {!gstPercentage}% or as applicable at the time of dispatch. The Party has to provide the GST No for both the buyer and consignee at the time of placing order.
                            <strong>7.b) TCS:</strong> As applicable extra @ {!tcsPercentage}%. Any changes in the statutory taxes at the time of dispatch will be charged as per the prevailing rates.
                        </div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">8. Payment Terms:</span> {!paymentTerms}</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">9. Interest:</span> In case of delay in making payment beyond the agreed period 24% interest per annum will be charged extra apart from other losses, if any.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">10. Ground Rent:</span> Material to be lifted within {!groundRentDays} days from the date of inspection/confirmation for lifting, if not lifted ground rental charges will be applicable @ {!groundRentPercentage}% per day.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">11. Validity:</span> This offer shall remain {!validityTerms} from the date of issuing of the present quotation thereafter with the efflux of time this offer shall deemed become null and void, unless the same is revalidated in writing.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">12. Delivery period &amp; Terms: </span> {!deliveryPeriod}</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">13. Penal interest:</span> In the event if the Buyer fails to make payment of the invoices raised within seven days and/or as may be agreed otherwise, from the date of receipt of the same in that event the Supplier shall be entitled to impose penal interest @24% per annum quarterly compoundable.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">14. Insurance:</span> {!insuranceTerms}</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">15. Service Charges (Erection &amp; other services):</span> Erection &amp; Commissioning is to be done by the buyer, unless otherwise specified/agreed in writing separate service charges will be applicable for any service required for supervision on erection &amp; commissioning. On receipt of buyer’s request, our service charge will be communicated.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">16. Breach &amp; Default:</span> If the Buyer or the Supplier fails to comply with the terms and conditions of this agreement in that event the defaulting party shall become liable to compensate the other party by way of damages, however such other party shall become entitled to claim damages provided such claim is duly substantiated with proper evidence.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">17. Late Delivery Charges:</span> Unless prevented by force majeure condition the Supplier shall be liable to deliver the materials within the agreed delivery schedule. However, since the Supplier has agreed to supply the materials at an extremely competitive rates it is being made clear that for the purpose of this contract the Buyer shall not be entitled to impose any late delivery charges for any delay caused in delivery of the materials.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">18. Price variation clause: </span> {!priceVariationClause}</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">19. Test Certificate:</span> {!testCertificate}</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">20. Short Supply:</span> As and when the materials are delivered at the agreed point of delivery, the Supplier shall not assume any responsibility or obligation to deal with any claims relating to short supply raised by the Buyer.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">21. Warranty:</span> The Supplier’s products are covered by a mechanical guarantee for a period of {!warrantyMonths} months from the date of commissioning or at the latest {!warrantyEndMonth} months from the date of delivery as per the agreed incoterm, unless a longer period has been accepted by the Supplier on case by case basis. The warranty period for a defective material, which has been replaced, shall extend only to the extent of the unexpired term of such warranty from the date of replacement. Repaired or corrected materials shall remain warranted for the balance of the original warranty period.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">22. Custody:</span> Once the materials are arrived at your site the same will remain under your custody for safe and secure storage.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">23. Quality:</span> In the event if the results of the pre-delivery inspection carried out at the behest of the Buyer are found to be in conflict with the findings of the inspection made at the Buyer’s destination, by any independent inspection agency and/or surveyor engaged by the Buyer, under such circumstances the Buyer shall have to provide a reasonable and acceptable explanation justifying the reason for such conflicting reports by two different independent agencies both being appointed by the Buyers. If the Buyer fails to substantiate the claim with proper and acceptable explanation in that eventthe Buyer’s claim on quality related issues shall stand set aside and/or determined.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">24. Return of Goods:</span> Be it noted that after obtaining satisfactory inspection clearance certification once the goods are sold and delivered the Buyer will not be entitled to return the same by raising any technical issues or defects.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">25. Force Majeure:</span> a) In this agreement, “force majeure” means any cause preventing Supplier from performing any or all of its obligations which arises from or is attributable to acts or events beyond the reasonable control of the party so prevented, including, without limitation, strikes, lock-outs or other industrial disputes (whether involving the workforce of the party so prevented or of any other party), act of god, war, riot, civil commotion, malicious damage, accident, breakdown of plant or machinery, fire, flood, storm or default of suppliers or sub-contractors. (b) If Supplier is prevented or delayed in the performance of any of its obligations under this contract by force majeure, that party shall forthwith serve notice in writing on the other party specifying the nature and extent of the circumstances giving rise to force majeure and subject to service of such notices such party shall have no liability in respect of the performance of such of its obligations as are prevented by the force majeure events during the continuation of such events and for such time after they cease as is necessary for that party, using all reasonable endeavours, to recommence its affected operations in order for it to perform its obligations. (c) If Supplier is prevented from performance of its obligations for a continuous period in excess of two months, the Buyer and/or the Supplier may terminate this agreement forthwith on service of written notice on the party so prevented, in which case neither party shall have any liability to the other except that rights and liabilities which accrued prior to such termination shall continue to subsist.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">26. Declaration:</span> Estimates given for total cost and material are based on drawing provided by the customer and we are not responsible if any deviation from drawing is found at the actual site.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">27. Arbitration &amp; Jurisdiction:</span> No suit or any proceedings in regard to any matter arising in respect of this contract shall be instituted in any court, save in the High Court, Calcutta, City Civil Court at Calcutta or at the Court of small causes at Calcutta. It is agreed that no other court shall have jurisdiction to entertain any suit or proceedings, even though, part of the cause of action might arise within their jurisdiction.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">28. Miscellaneous:</span> Not withstanding anything otherwise or contrary recorded anywhere within the purchase/supply order arising from this quotation, the terms and conditions of this quotation shall be deemed to be a part of the consequent supply order and/or contract and in the event of any conflict in interpretation of the clauses of this quotation in that event the clauses of the quotation shall prevail over the clauses of the purchase/supply order.</div>
                        <div class="term-item"><span class="term-title">29. Confidentiality:</span> The terms and conditions described in this contract including its existence shall be confidential information and shall not be disclosed by any party to any third party without the prior written consent of the other party. Each of the Parties agrees, (unless otherwise required by law), that it shall not disclose to any other person the fact that the confidential information has been made available to the other party, that discussions or negotiations are taking place concerning the said enquiry/tender proceedings between the Parties, or any of the terms, conditions or other facts with respect thereto (including the status thereof).</div>
                        
